+## ☁️ Deployment
+
+> **Note:** This is a Java Spring Boot server. It **cannot run on Vercel or Netlify** (they only host static sites / Node serverless functions). Use a platform that runs Docker or Java.
+
+### Render (recommended, free tier)
+1. Push this repo to GitHub.
+2. On [render.com](https://render.com) → **New → Blueprint** → select this repo (it reads `render.yaml`).
+   Or **New → Web Service** → choose the repo → Runtime: **Docker**.
+3. Deploy. Render sets `PORT` automatically; the app listens on it.
+
+### Railway / Fly.io / any Docker host
+The included `Dockerfile` builds and runs the app:
+```bash
+docker build -t nlp-platform .
+docker run -p 8080:8080 nlp-platform
+```
+
+### Environment variables
+| Variable | Purpose | Default |
+|---|---|---|
+| `PORT` | HTTP port | `8080` |
+| `DB_URL` | JDBC URL (use MySQL in production) | H2 file at `./data/nlp_db` |
+| `DB_USERNAME` / `DB_PASSWORD` | DB credentials | `sa` / `password` |
+| `DB_DRIVER` | e.g. `com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver` | `org.h2.Driver` |
+| `DB_DIALECT` | e.g. `org.hibernate.dialect.MySQLDialect` | `org.hibernate.dialect.H2Dialect` |
+| `H2_CONSOLE_ENABLED` | Set `false` in production | `true` |
+
+⚠️ On free hosting tiers the container disk is wiped on every redeploy/restart, so the default H2 file database will reset. For data that persists, set the `DB_*` variables to a hosted MySQL database.
+
